  "id": "DrugBank_DB00515 - MONDO_16248",
  "verbalization": "Cisplatin is being considered for repositioning in the treatment of Familial Ovarian Cancer based on its association with Immature Ovarian Teratoma, a condition that is linked to Familial Ovarian Cancer through a series of indications. The evidence suggests that Cisplatin may exert a therapeutic effect through a shared pathway involving Immature Ovarian Teratoma, which in turn is associated with Familial Ovarian Cancer. This pathway involves the use of alternative drugs like Altretamine and Rucaparib, which are also linked to Familial Ovarian Cancer, indicating a potential mechanistic overlap. The presence of multiple indirect pathways connecting Cisplatin to Familial Ovarian Cancer supports the hypothesis that the drug may act through a mechanism that influences cellular processes relevant to ovarian cancer development. The integration of these pathways suggests that Cisplatin could be repositioned to target a shared biological process in Familial Ovarian Cancer, though further mechanistic validation is required to confirm the exact role of Cisplatin in this context.",
